1
00:00:13,496 --> 00:00:14,337
Peace and joy.

2
00:00:14,378 --> 00:00:15,699
Good evening to you all.

3
00:00:16,021 --> 00:00:17,422
I hope you've had a fruitful day.

4
00:00:17,443 --> 00:00:18,504
I don't say happy.

5
00:00:18,524 --> 00:00:20,788
I hope it has been a happy day.

6
00:00:20,829 --> 00:00:37,615
Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambho Tassa Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambho Tassa

7
00:00:38,253 --> 00:00:47,002
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambuddhasa.

8
00:00:47,021 --> 00:00:53,848
Homage to the Buddha, the blessed, noble and fully self-awakened one.

9
00:00:53,868 --> 00:00:58,433
I have to be careful I've got the microphone on.

10
00:00:58,454 --> 00:01:04,680
Okay, so we're moving on to a different discourse.

11
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,522
This is the Wanderer Vaikunasa.

12
00:01:07,834 --> 00:01:13,322
It's a bit strange, this conversation, but try and make some head or tail of it.

13
00:01:14,123 --> 00:01:15,825
Anyway, he's a Samana.

14
00:01:15,924 --> 00:01:18,947
He's somebody who's left the home life, the homeless life.

15
00:01:19,649 --> 00:01:26,757
And he approaches the Buddha after the usual greetings and all that and says, this is the perfect splendor.

16
00:01:26,957 --> 00:01:28,579
This is the perfect splendor.

17
00:01:29,501 --> 00:01:31,522
And the Buddha says, what do you mean?

18
00:01:31,643 --> 00:01:32,965
What do you actually mean by that?

19
00:01:33,367 --> 00:01:41,621
And he replies, Master Gautama, this splendor is the perfect splendor which is unsurpassed by any other splendor higher or more sublime.

20
00:01:42,582 --> 00:01:48,733
And the Buddha says, well, what exactly is this splendor which is unsurpassed that you're talking about?

21
00:01:49,615 --> 00:01:58,311
And Kachana says, that splendor is the perfect splendor that is unsurpassed by any other splendor higher and more sublime.

22
00:01:58,628 --> 00:02:25,227
and uh the buddha says you could you could carry on like this for a very long time now there's a story now uh well uh a metaphor which the body uses it does occur in other discourses so i don't quite know uh which discourse it actually uh arrives in first see if i can find this one oh i've taken the

23
00:02:26,201 --> 00:02:34,930
It's the sutta before, actually.

24
00:02:40,336 --> 00:02:41,836
Too many suttas, that's the problem.

25
00:02:41,896 --> 00:02:42,818
Too many discourses.

26
00:02:45,961 --> 00:02:46,300
Okay.

27
00:02:46,981 --> 00:02:53,068
So the Buddha then says, you can continue like this for a very long time.

28
00:02:54,568 --> 00:02:55,449
Venerable, that

29
00:02:55,953 --> 00:03:06,245
So he says, it's like somebody who says, I am in love with the most beautiful woman in the country.

30
00:03:07,045 --> 00:03:12,812
And they would ask, good man, the most beautiful woman in the country, with whom are you in love?

31
00:03:13,592 --> 00:03:15,115
I don't know, he says, I don't know.

32
00:03:15,795 --> 00:03:19,740
He says, well, is it from this country or from another country?

33
00:03:19,879 --> 00:03:20,661
I don't know.

34
00:03:20,961 --> 00:03:22,283
What's her name?

35
00:03:22,364 --> 00:03:22,884
Her clan?

36
00:03:23,085 --> 00:03:23,686
I don't know.

37
00:03:23,825 --> 00:03:24,507
Is she tall?

38
00:03:24,546 --> 00:03:25,187
Is she short?

39
00:03:25,268 --> 00:03:26,229
Is she middle height?

40
00:03:26,729 --> 00:03:27,350
I don't know.

41
00:03:27,872 --> 00:03:30,155
What village or town or city does she live in?

42
00:03:30,194 --> 00:03:30,735
I don't know.

43
00:03:30,776 --> 00:03:35,723
Then they would ask him, good man, do you then love a girl you've never known or seen?

44
00:03:35,763 --> 00:03:36,824
Yes.

45
00:03:37,324 --> 00:03:38,385
And he said, what do you think?

46
00:03:38,967 --> 00:03:43,332
That being so, would that man's talk amount to nonsense?

47
00:03:43,353 --> 00:03:50,242
So, of course, he has to agree that, in fact, this would be nonsense.

48
00:03:51,639 --> 00:04:10,806
And then somehow, not quite know where the connection is, but the Buddha either intuits or begins to understand that the problem here is that Vekanasa, that's his name actually, Vekanasa, really means the five sensual pleasures.

49
00:04:10,926 --> 00:04:15,133
That's the five physical bodily pleasures, not the mental ones.

50
00:04:16,226 --> 00:04:21,672
So then he gives the usual discussion, teaching about that.

51
00:04:22,411 --> 00:04:34,562
Those things that are cognizable by the eye are wished for, desired, agreeable and likable, connected with sensual desire or greed or avarice and so on and so forth.

52
00:04:34,583 --> 00:04:37,706
And that's the same for all the other four senses.

53
00:04:37,805 --> 00:04:41,629
These are the five chords of sensual pleasure.

54
00:04:44,012 --> 00:04:44,411
Now,

55
00:04:44,543 --> 00:04:50,848
Pleasure and joy that arise dependent on this, on sensual pleasure, is called sensual pleasure.

56
00:04:51,528 --> 00:05:00,276
And sensual pleasure through the pleasures, but beyond sensual pleasure, there is a pleasure higher than sensual pleasure, and this is to be declared the highest among them.

57
00:05:01,057 --> 00:05:05,762
So the Buddha is saying here that, of course, there are pleasures and joys way above it.

58
00:05:06,242 --> 00:05:12,728
Now, the odd thing about this is that this man is a samana, so he's left the home life,

59
00:05:13,096 --> 00:05:27,072
which is normally described as that which is indulging in the five sense pleasures, and he's left to become a a recluse, an ascetic.

60
00:05:27,514 --> 00:05:37,146
So it's difficult to know how he's satisfying it, except that it was fairly well known in those days, as unfortunately it is today,

61
00:05:37,430 --> 00:05:44,238
that anybody passing themselves off as a holy man or as a guru can sometimes get their way with women.

62
00:05:44,759 --> 00:05:50,786
And as you know, we've had some pretty bad cases in the total Buddhist community.

63
00:05:52,168 --> 00:05:55,713
So I presume that's what he's on about.

64
00:05:56,233 --> 00:06:04,584
So anyway, Vaikhanatha sort of says, oh, well, that's really good teaching, you see, if for some reason he hadn't thought of that before.

65
00:06:04,851 --> 00:06:27,725
And then Kacana, the Buddha goes on, for you who are of another view, who accept another teaching, who approve another teaching, who pursue a different training, who follow a different teacher, it is hard to know what sensuality is, or what sensual pleasure is, or what the pleasure higher than the sensual is.

66
00:06:28,485 --> 00:06:30,588
But those bhikkhus who are Arahats,

67
00:06:30,822 --> 00:06:36,009
And then the usual description of an arahant, somebody who's destroyed the fetters of being, etc.

68
00:06:36,649 --> 00:06:42,656
They know what sensuality is, what sensual pleasure is, and what pleasure higher than the sensual is.

69
00:06:43,137 --> 00:06:50,608
Now, for some reason, this upsets Vaikhanasa, because obviously the Buddha is saying you simply wouldn't understand.

70
00:06:50,648 --> 00:06:52,290
So I suppose it is understandable.

71
00:06:52,725 --> 00:07:03,379
So Vaikhanatha is angry and displeased and he reviled and disparaged and censured the Buddha, the Blessed One, saying the recluse Gautama will be worsted.

72
00:07:05,401 --> 00:07:16,134
So then the Blessed One says, there are some recluses and Brahmins who, without knowing the past and without seeing the future, birth is destroyed.

73
00:07:16,468 --> 00:07:35,257
Sorry, then Vaikhanatha says to the Buddha, so there are some recluses and Brahmins here who without knowing the past and without seeing the future yet claim birth is destroyed, the holy life is lived, what had to be done has been done.

74
00:07:35,697 --> 00:07:39,523
So it's the usual description of someone who has gone beyond.

75
00:07:40,093 --> 00:07:48,182
What they say then turns out to be mere words, empty and hollow, according to you, you know, the blessed one.

76
00:07:48,201 --> 00:08:03,057
So the Buddha replies, if any recluses of Brahmins without knowing the past and without seeing the future yet claim birth is destroyed, et cetera, et cetera, they can be proven wrong in accordance with the Dharma.

77
00:08:03,958 --> 00:08:06,220
Let the past be, Kachana.

78
00:08:06,502 --> 00:08:07,783
and let the future be.

79
00:08:08,004 --> 00:08:12,509
Let a wise man come who is honest, sincere, a man of rectitude.

80
00:08:13,088 --> 00:08:14,009
I will instruct him.

81
00:08:14,110 --> 00:08:21,036
I teach him the Dharma in such a way that by practicing as instructed, he will soon know and see for himself.

82
00:08:22,278 --> 00:08:29,865
This indeed, there rightly comes to be liberation from the bond, that is, the bond of ignorance.

83
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:35,429
Now, suppose, Kachana, there was a young, tender infant, lying prone, bound in

84
00:08:35,578 --> 00:08:36,941
in swaddling clothes.

85
00:08:38,522 --> 00:08:46,331
And later on, as a result of growth and maturing of his faculties, those swaddlings were loosened.

86
00:08:46,552 --> 00:08:51,157
And he would know, I am free, and there would be no more bondage.

87
00:08:51,677 --> 00:08:53,600
So it is with the wise man.

88
00:08:54,279 --> 00:08:56,802
Now, Vivekananda is really taken by this.

89
00:08:56,883 --> 00:08:59,687
And he says, magnificent, Master Gautama, magnificent.

90
00:09:00,346 --> 00:09:02,649
Those who have eyes to see, et cetera, et cetera.

91
00:09:03,110 --> 00:09:05,332
And from today, the Blessed One will remember me

92
00:09:05,481 --> 00:09:07,865
as a lay follower who's gone forth refuge.

93
00:09:08,285 --> 00:09:15,235
So he's actually, he comes in as a wanderer and he leaves as a lay person.

94
00:09:15,716 --> 00:09:20,023
So he's obviously thought twice about his, about the way he's living as a wanderer.

95
00:09:20,845 --> 00:09:35,285
Now, uh, the question for me that arises when, when, uh, when we talk about sensual pleasure is, um, is direct is to ask ourselves, is it the actual sensual pleasure that we want?

96
00:09:36,245 --> 00:09:47,476
So when you're eating something, if it were just the sensual pleasure of eating, just the sheer taste, would that be enough?

97
00:09:48,018 --> 00:09:50,640
So we have to eat.

98
00:09:50,681 --> 00:09:53,322
We have to eat at least once a day.

99
00:09:53,443 --> 00:09:56,125
I'm sure many people eat many more times.

100
00:09:56,767 --> 00:09:57,888
I also have breakfast.

101
00:09:59,450 --> 00:10:04,075
But the question is, when we eat

102
00:10:04,392 --> 00:10:22,249
something or hear something or see something which is beautiful attractive etc would that simple sensual pleasure be enough you see now i i would suggest that what comes with it is a mental state and that mental state

103
00:10:22,533 --> 00:10:25,095
is variously described as happiness.

104
00:10:25,556 --> 00:10:38,327
There's all levels and types of happiness, from a sense of comfort, a sense of joy, a sense of wonder, all those beautiful mental states, we can describe them as happiness.

105
00:10:39,087 --> 00:10:49,738
So the question is, do we actually want the object of sensual pleasure or do we want the sensual pleasure in order to create the inner mental state of happiness?

106
00:10:50,917 --> 00:10:52,379
That's where the connection is.

107
00:10:52,519 --> 00:10:54,442
That's where the connection can go wrong.

108
00:10:54,902 --> 00:11:02,972
Because then this happiness becomes dependent on what it is that the sensual pleasure is giving us.

109
00:11:03,173 --> 00:11:06,297
Whatever the sensual pleasure is giving us becomes dependent.

110
00:11:06,317 --> 00:11:09,701
That dependency is what we call attachment.

111
00:11:09,801 --> 00:11:10,743
It's a dependency.

112
00:11:10,763 --> 00:11:12,043
It's like any drug.

113
00:11:12,664 --> 00:11:16,570
So then our practice is to be constantly aware of that.

114
00:11:16,971 --> 00:11:21,056
You can't get rid of conditioning just because you want to get rid of it.

115
00:11:21,397 --> 00:11:32,927
You have to be aware of it, that, oh, yeah, okay, this is greed, this is avarice, this is lust, this is the desire for power, whatever it is that turns you on.

116
00:11:33,509 --> 00:11:44,019
And to see that clearly, you see, and then, of course, you have to wait for that to pass or at least not purposefully activate it, purposefully activate it.

117
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,201
And then we go back.

118
00:11:46,418 --> 00:11:54,957
and use the original sensual pleasure as just sensual pleasure.

119
00:11:55,438 --> 00:12:00,090
Now, when you use just sensual pleasure as sensual pleasure,

120
00:12:00,273 --> 00:12:04,837
The heart still responds, but the dependence is not there.

121
00:12:04,857 --> 00:12:05,077
See?

122
00:12:05,438 --> 00:12:09,222
So it's a case of learning how to let go.

123
00:12:09,263 --> 00:12:18,312
Every time something comes to us that we are grasping onto is to recognize the grasp and then just let it go.

124
00:12:18,753 --> 00:12:20,774
Just keep dropping it all the time.

125
00:12:21,576 --> 00:12:30,144
And that way, of course, you fulfill, I've quoted Blake before, but this lovely phrase from Blake, to kiss the joy as it flies,

126
00:12:30,394 --> 00:12:32,277
is to live in eternity's sunrise.

127
00:12:33,077 --> 00:12:37,962
So I think that's something that we can take from this particular discourse.

128
00:12:39,745 --> 00:12:42,427
But it's a funny opening to it.

129
00:12:42,908 --> 00:12:48,394
He goes around saying this is the highest and most wonderful thing, but he can't tell the Buddha what it is.

130
00:12:49,335 --> 00:12:51,998
Anyway, by the end of it, of course, he's found his feet.

131
00:12:52,618 --> 00:12:57,043
And it's interesting that he goes back to the household life.

132
00:12:57,884 --> 00:12:59,869
So just a little tale there.

133
00:13:00,129 --> 00:13:02,254
I hope you find it inspirational.

134
00:13:02,895 --> 00:13:09,812
I hope it drives you on towards full liberation from suffering sooner rather than later.

135
00:13:12,399 --> 00:13:14,003
So we can do some practice.

